WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.602
Evidence can conflict.

00:00:01.602 --> 00:00:09.437
Suppose one policy says the return window is fourteen days, while another says thirty days during a holiday period.

00:00:09.437 --> 00:00:14.058
The system should not silently choose the chunk that gives the easiest answer.

00:00:14.626 --> 00:00:19.053
Instead, inspect metadata. Which policy is current?

00:00:19.053 --> 00:00:22.403
Does the holiday exception apply to the purchase date?

00:00:22.403 --> 00:00:25.028
Which source has higher authority?

00:00:25.028 --> 00:00:27.883
Is one document an older version?

00:00:27.883 --> 00:00:32.161
This is where provenance and structured metadata become very important.

00:00:32.611 --> 00:00:39.933
Resolve source conflicts before asking the language model to synthesize the final answer whenever possible.

00:00:39.933 --> 00:00:46.498
The model is better at explaining a resolved policy than deciding which business rule is legally or operationally

00:00:46.498 --> 00:00:48.659
authoritative.
